# bus_storage and document_store consolidate into ONE store, ONE face [SPEC:CXC-STORE]

> **PLACEMENT RATIFIED, AUDIT PASSED, LANDED.** This document captured a design decision reached
> in conversation and was held for an INDEPENDENT design-audit before landing — the same
> self-certification guard [CXC-BUSSTORE-CONVERSION-STATUS] applies to a code-conversion pass
> applies here to a decision-conversion pass: the author of a decision does not get to be its
> only reviewer. That audit — a three-agent design-diamond (gap-analyzer + first-bringup + qa) —
> RAN and PASSED with ZERO MUST violations; its findings are applied throughout this document
> (v0.3, below). Placement is now RATIFIED into `corpora/platform-specs/`
> ([CXC-STORE-PLACEMENT]) — 92 was the first free numeric prefix, chosen by listing, not
> counting. The code implementing this decision has LANDED on origin/main.
>
> `lifecycle-position` says the same thing a query can read: **`committed — diamond-verified
> (gap-analyzer + first-bringup + qa, zero MUST violations), landed on origin/main`**.

---

## 0. The decision, its provenance, and placement

### [DEC-STORAGE-CONSOLIDATE-ONE-FACE] bus_storage SURVIVES, document_store is KILLED, the store exposes ONE face — bus://

- decision: bus_storage and document_store are collapsed into ONE store. bus_storage SURVIVES as the store; document_store is KILLED — its service, its ComposeServer plugin, its SQLite doc DB and its second containment guard are all removed. The store exposes a SINGLE face, `bus://` (path-addressed bytes/blobs). The `doc://` scheme and its server-side query engine are RETIRED (see `doc-scheme-retirement-scope` — "retired" is qualified, not unqualified gone).
- doc-scheme-retirement-scope: "RETIRED" means the WIRE face is ONE — `bus://` — and no `doc://` reaches any `:8421` path, because document_store is killed; the one-face MUST is MET. `doc://` SURVIVES as a client-side read-time compat alias: `python/composeio/resolve.py`'s `resolve_doc` (via its `_doc_to_bus` translator) and `render/engine/assets.py` translate a `doc://<collection>/<id>` string to `bus://<collection>/<id>.json` at resolve time, because stored documents may still carry `doc://` cross-references. This alias does NOT rewrite in-doc cross-references — `tools/migrate_document_store_to_bus.py` copies each migrated JSON document's `data` verbatim (re-serialized, not field-rewritten) — so a `doc://` string embedded inside a document (e.g. an app doc's `surface` field) is PERMANENT until an OPTIONAL cutover cross-reference-rewrite pass runs; see [CXC-STORE-CUTOVER-XREF-REWRITE]. Diamond finding: gap-analyzer P1 + qa note 3, 2026-09-02.
- why-one-face-not-two: David's stated reason, in his own plain terms rather than technical framing — a "not dual-interface" preference: "we'd be keeping bus://" (transcript L30858).
- why-one-face-not-two-architect-framing: the architect's added technical justification for the same conclusion, not David's words — a dual `bus://` + `doc://` interface is a narrow-waist violation, two faces over one primitive being exactly the N×M fan-out [DX-NARROW-WAIST] exists to prevent, when N+M (one face, capabilities that need it extended to meet it) was available.
- why-bus_storage-survives: named directly in [CXC-STORE-EVIDENCE-SCALE] — it is the live, load-bearing store; document_store's catalog is thin by comparison and its distinguishing capability (server-side query) is disposed of separately in [DD-STORE-QUERY-DISPOSITION] rather than carried forward as a reason to keep it as the survivor.
- http-face-discrepancy-omitted: moot because we're deprecating document_store; revisit ONLY if the deprecation is reversed (David 2026-09-03).
- provenance: david-ruling, transcript L30807 ("kill doc_storage altogether") and L30858 ("we'd be keeping bus://").
- dsd-source: docs/architecture/DSD-storage-consolidation.md
- lifecycle-position: committed — diamond-verified (gap-analyzer + first-bringup + qa, zero MUST violations), landed on origin/main.
- supersedes: [DEC-DOCSTORE-BUS-QUERY-FACE]
- see-also: [DX-NARROW-WAIST]
- see-also: [DX-COLLAPSE-TRANSPORT]
- see-also: [SPEC:CXC-BUSSTORE]
- see-also: [CXC-DOCSTORE]
- see-also: [CXC-BUS-QUERY]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-STORE]

### [CXC-STORE-PLACEMENT] Placement is RATIFIED — the spec stays in platform-specs/, and 92 was chosen by listing rather than by counting

- placement-status: RATIFIED (architect's call, 2026-09-02, following the design-diamond's PASS). The spec stays filed in `corpora/platform-specs/`. Rationale: this document is a SPEC carrying evidence slots, a consumer census, and pre-/post-integration questions — not merely a decision node, so it does not belong filed with the decision graph alone; its dependencies (`73-bus-storage.lts`, `82-document-store-containment.lts`, `86-composebus-request-response.lts`) all live in `platform-specs/`; and spec 73, [SPEC:CXC-BUSSTORE], already set the precedent of a service spec filed there ([CXC-BUSSTORE-PLACEMENT]).
- number-chosen: 92. The directory was listed; 00-91 and 99 are taken, 92 is the first free prefix.
- ratification-resolved: whether this decision belongs filed alongside service specs at all, or whether it should live with the decision graph it supersedes/amends instead — RESOLVED above, by the architect, as part of the design-audit this document was gated on: `platform-specs/`, for the reasons in `placement-status`.
- see-also: [CXC-VISION-PLACEMENT]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-STORE]

