## 5. Supersessions and amendments into the decision graph

### [CXC-STORE-SUPERSESSION-NOTE] What this decision supersedes and amends, and why

- supersedes-docstore-bus-query-face: [DEC-DOCSTORE-BUS-QUERY-FACE] decided document_store gets a bus query face, additive to its HTTP API. That decision is MOOT once document_store is killed — there is no HTTP API left for a bus face to be additive TO, and the request/response idiom it established ([CXC-BUS-QUERY-IDIOM]) survives independently as platform vocabulary, per [CXC-BUS-QUERY]'s own framing as "the platform's FIRST request/response idiom... other query services will copy." The idiom is not retired; the decision to build it specifically for document_store's HTTP-additive face is.
- amends-private-host-plugin-topology: [DEC-(a private host name, not published)-HOST-STORAGE-AS-PLUGINS-DAY-ONE-2026-09-02] decided ComposeServer on COMPOSEIO_MQTT_BROKER hosts bus_storage / document_store / fingerprint_template_store (+ time) as per-tenant plugins. This decision AMENDS that topology: document_store is no longer hosted-as-a-plugin — it is killed. Only bus_storage, fingerprint_template_store, and time remain plugins under that decision's topology.
- moots-the-plugin-http-face-question: the document_store-plugin HTTP-face question (additive-vs-bus-native) that [DEC-(a private host name, not published)-HOST-STORAGE-AS-PLUGINS-DAY-ONE-2026-09-02] left open is thereby MOOT — there is no document_store plugin left to carry an HTTP face.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-STORE]

### [CXC-STORE-DOCSTORE-PLUGIN-QUESTION-MOOT] The document_store-plugin HTTP-face question is moot

- moot-because: [DEC-(a private host name, not published)-HOST-STORAGE-AS-PLUGINS-DAY-ONE-2026-09-02] left open whether a hosted document_store plugin's HTTP face should be additive-vs-bus-native. With document_store killed under [DEC-STORAGE-CONSOLIDATE-ONE-FACE], there is no document_store plugin left to carry that question — it is moot, not answered.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-STORE]

