## 6. Pre-integration questions — for the design-audit and for cutover

### [CXC-STORE-PRE-CENSUS] Has a live-traffic census on :8421 confirmed no external consumer before the kill?

- question: EMPTY. A live-traffic census on `:8421`, using the logging-tarpit approach already adopted for the (a private host name, not published) migration ([DEC-(a private host name, not published)-ADOPT-LOGGING-TARPIT] — 410 Gone + log every request), has not yet been run against document_store's port. This must catch any consumer outside [CXC-STORE-CONSUMER-SEAMS] / [CXC-STORE-CONSUMERS] before the kill proceeds.
- see-also: [DEC-(a private host name, not published)-ADOPT-LOGGING-TARPIT]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-STORE]

### [CXC-STORE-PRE-SECRETS] Does the unified store's access model account for secrets already living in assets? — QA finding recorded, flagged for David at cutover

- question: RECORDED (diamond qa note 2, 2026-09-02) — no longer EMPTY, but NOT resolved: this is a DAVID-decision item for the cutover access model, not a land-blocker. The new `/api/v1/blob/<path>` route is rooted at `BLOB_ROOT = DATA_DIR` — the WHOLE data directory — reached through the SAME single `_resolve_contained` containment guard as every other route. That WIDENS the pre-existing unauthenticated surface this node and [CXC-BUSSTORE-PRE-AUTH] already park: the blob route can GET/PUT/DELETE anywhere under `DATA_DIR`, including `configs/`, `assets/` (and so `assets/fleet/private/*.creds`), and `namespace_registry.json` — not only the 10 real doc collections. Separately, `PUT /api/v1/blob/configs/<id>.bin` writes a device config while BYPASSING the dedicated config route's `.meta.json` checksum-metadata sidecar — `_handle_config_put`'s `X-ComposeIO-Metadata` header handling has no equivalent in `_handle_blob_put`.
- not-a-land-blocker-because: no spec clause forbids rooting the blob route at DATA_DIR, and the 10 real collection names (apps, surfaces, board_profiles, components, bsg_planets, recipes, fleet_devices, …) do not collide with `configs/` / `assets/` / `workloads/`, so nothing breaks today. Containment itself holds — `_resolve_contained` still refuses traversal. This is an ACCESS-MODEL question for cutover, not a containment defect.
- flagged-for: David, at the cutover access-model decision — whether the blob route should refuse `configs/` and `assets/fleet/private/` (or require auth) before the store carries live secrets at scale.
- see-also: [CXC-BUSSTORE-PRE-AUTH]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-STORE]

