## 7. Post-integration evidence slots — EMPTY until something real fills them

### [CXC-STORE-EV-01] Every consumer in [CXC-STORE-CONSUMER-SEAMS], [CXC-STORE-CONSUMER-SEAMS-YAML] and [CXC-STORE-CONSUMERS] repoints and round-trips against the unified store

- evidence: EMPTY.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-STORE]

### [CXC-STORE-EV-02] The fresh verified copy at cutover matches document_store's live count, not a stale snapshot's

- evidence: EMPTY. Falsifiable against [CXC-STORE-DATA-ABSORPTION]'s near-nil-caveat: 46 docs / 10 collections / 26 blobs, verified against the LIVE writer, not a count that merely happens to match. Verification standard per `byte-identity-precision`: BINARY byte-identical for the blobs, JSON SEMANTICALLY-identical for the docs — do not require byte-identity of the re-serialized JSON.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-STORE]

### [CXC-STORE-CUTOVER-XREF-REWRITE] Optional cutover step — rewrite in-doc doc:// cross-references to bus://

- status: OPTIONAL, not required to satisfy the one-face MUST — the wire already carries one face regardless (see [DEC-STORAGE-CONSOLIDATE-ONE-FACE]'s `doc-scheme-retirement-scope`).
- what: a pass over migrated documents that rewrites embedded `doc://<collection>/<id>` cross-reference strings (e.g. an app doc's `surface` field) to `bus://<collection>/<id>.json`, so the compat alias in `resolve.py` / `assets.py` stops being load-bearing at read time.
- why-optional: `resolve_doc` / `_doc_to_bus` already translate `doc://` at read time and will keep doing so correctly and permanently; this step only retires the alias's necessity, it does not fix a defect.
- when: EV-02-adjacent — natural to run alongside the fresh verified copy at cutover ([CXC-STORE-EV-02]), since both touch the migrated document set, but it is a SEPARATE, optional pass, not a precondition of EV-02.
- see-also: [CXC-STORE-EV-02]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-STORE]

### [CXC-STORE-EV-03] The :8421 census in [CXC-STORE-PRE-CENSUS] ran and found no consumer outside the named migration surface

- evidence: EMPTY.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-STORE]

### [CXC-STORE-EV-04] DocPicker's client-side filter is functionally equivalent to the dropped server-side query, at current scale

- evidence: EMPTY. Falsifiable against [DD-STORE-QUERY-DISPOSITION]: the same `where`-shaped queries `DocPicker` issues today must return the same results filtered client-side, over the same 46-doc / 5-doc-largest-collection store.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-STORE]

